// The WP-010 movement test field. Y is up; the player spawns at the origin facing +Z.
// Features (docs/game/02-world.md, "Traversal and world mechanics"):
//   - Slope: in the lane x = -14..14 the ground ramps from 0 m at z = 10 to 9 m at
//     z = 28 (26.6 degrees, under the 45 degree climb limit), then is flat to z = 30.
//   - Steep ridge: x = 20..28, z = -6..-4 rises 4 m over 2 m (63 degrees), too steep
//     to walk up.
//   - Steps: four 0.3 m steps at x = -26..-20 starting at z = 2.6, each 0.6 m deep,
//     under the 0.4 m autostep. The top step continues to z = 10.
//   - Ledge: the "ledge" box rises 1 m above the top of the ramp at z = 30, too high to
//     step up, low enough to jump (1.1 m jump height).
//   - Drop: the far edge of the ledge box, at z = 40, is a 10 m drop to flat ground.
// Heightfield: 33 columns by 49 rows of vertices, 2 m apart, covering x from -32 to 32
// and z from -32 to 64. Each line below is one row (one z value), listing heights from
// x = -32 to x = 32. Past the edges is the void (kill_y).
(
  spawn: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
  spawn_yaw: 0.0,
  kill_y: -50.0,
